From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:26:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 92/99] v8: e2k: wasm SIMD operations that e2k-v5 has whole

The code generator and Liftoff (copies of loong64) build a number of wasm
SIMD operations of LSX chains, which the layer turns into longer e2k ones.
For these e2k has one to four qp operations, now instructions of the layer
that are not LoongArch (la_asm.h), called directly:

- v128.const and i8x16.shuffle: the constant in two operations (vconst),
  the shuffle one qppermb (vperm_b) instead of 15;
- narrowing with saturation: one qpack* (vpackss/vpackus) instead of 13;
- bitmask: qpsgn2mskb after packing (vmsk_*) instead of 10;
- q15mulr_sat_s: qpmulhrsh with the 0x8000 case (vq15mulr_h);
- abs (qpsign x, x), dot_i16x8_s (qpmaddh);
- shifts by a register without splatting the count (v*_<s>r);
- f32x4/f64x2 min, max (vwmin/vwmax, NaN and -0 as wasm), pmin, pmax
  (one qpfmin/qpfmax).
